:"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pXwL2","user":{"login":"Delsin-Yu","id":71481700,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDgxNzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71481700?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu","html_url":"https://github.com/Delsin-Yu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-30T10:47:32Z","updated_at":"2025-04-30T10:49:44Z","body":"I have downloaded the MRP and tested it against the latest main branch [8edf97e34] with dotMemory. In case anyone needs a more specific GC pattern.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b5d0a20a-7616-436f-ba7c-8b3b56963088)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2841576182/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2841599789","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105750#issuecomment-2841599789","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105750","id":2841599789,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pX18t","user":{"login":"Delsin-Yu","id":71481700,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDgxNzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71481700?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu","html_url":"https://github.com/Delsin-Yu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-30T10:57:08Z","updated_at":"2025-04-30T11:00:45Z","body":"There are different approaches to solving the GC overhead issues you mentioned.\n\nFor StringName conversion allocations in the performance hotspot:\n```csharp\nbool res = Input.IsActionPressed(\"ui_accept\");\n```\nWe can either:\n1. Implement a Roslyn analyzer that checks for specific common usages that may create GC overhead and warn & provide a quick fix to the user.\n```\nGDXXXX: Replace implicit immediate string literals with cached StringName.\n```\n2. Implement a source generator that generates interceptor calls that redirect the invocation from `Input.IsActionPressed(StringName)` to another specifically written method `Input.IsActionPressedCached(string)` that does automatic StringName caching.\n\nFor the method that returns arrays or Godot collections:\n```csharp\nvar targets = this.GetTree().GetNodesInGroup(groupName);\n```\nWe can modify the binding generator to create an overload method that fills the result values into an additional `ICollection` parameter.\n```csharp\nprivate readonly List<Node> _cache = [];\n\npublic override void _Process(double delta)\n{\n    _cache.Clear();\n    this.GetTree().GetNodesInGroup(groupName, _cache);\n    // Use _cache\n}\n\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2841599789/reactions","total_count":6,"+1":6,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2841651624","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105750#issuecomment-2841651624","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105750","id":2841651624,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pYCmo","user":{"login":"Delsin-Yu","id":71481700,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDgxNzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71481700?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu","html_url":"https://github.com/Delsin-Yu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-30T11:15:26Z","updated_at":"2025-04-30T11:22:35Z","body":"By the way,\n\n> but I'm talking about calling them once per frame.\n\n***ONCE PER FRAME*** is considered a hot path.\n\nBut I admit that we should have a section in C# that emphasizes this to the user, like [what's done by Unity](https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/performance-garbage-collector.html), despite Godot using a .NET runtime that has a way stronger GC mechanism.\n\n> ## Temporary allocations\n> It’s common for an application to allocate temporary data to the [managed heap](https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/performance-managed-memory-introduction.html) in each frame but temporary allocations can affect the performance of the application.\n> For example, if a program allocates 1 KB of temporary memory each frame, and it runs at 60 frames per second, then it must allocate 60 KB of temporary memory per second. Over the course of a minute, this adds up to 3.6 MB of memory available to the garbage collector.\n> Invoking the garbage collector once per second has a negative effect on performance. If it has to clean up 3.6 MB spread across thousands of individual allocations, that might result in significant garbage collection times.\n> Loading operations have an impact on performance. If your application generates a lot of temporary objects during a heavy asset-loading operation, and Unity references those objects until the operation completes, then the garbage collector can’t release those temporary objects. This means that the managed heap needs to expand, even though Unity releases a lot of the objects that it contains a short time later.\n> To avoid managed heap expansion, reduce the amount of frequent managed heap allocations as possible: ideally to ***0 bytes per frame, or as close to zero as you can get.*** For information on how to optimize for managed heap allocations, refer to [Optimizing your code for managed memory](https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/performance-optimizing-code-managed-memory.html).\n\n> ## Optimizing your code for managed memory\n> Automatic memory management allows you to write code quickly and with few errors. However, this convenience might have performance implications. To optimize your code for performance, you must avoid situations where your application triggers the [garbage collector](https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/performance-garbage-collector.html) a lot. This section outlines some common issues and workflows that affect when your application triggers the garbage collector.\n> [Reference type management](https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/performance-reference-types.html)\n> - Optimize how you use reference types in your code.\n> \n> [Creating reusable code](https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/performance-reusable-code.html)\n> - Reuse code to optimize the performance of your application.\n> \n> [Optimizing arrays](https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/performance-optimizing-arrays.html)\n> - Optimize when and how you use arrays in your code.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2841651624/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2842356388","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105750#issuecomment-2842356388","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105750","id":2842356388,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pauqk","user":{"login":"beicause","id":75941842,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1OTQxODQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75941842?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause","html_url":"https://github.com/beicause","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-30T15:20:46Z","updated_at":"2025-05-02T16:04:28Z","body":"Tested on Linux, Godot 4.5, .NET SDK 9.0.105, .NET Runtime 9.0.4. I‘m unable to reproduce such serious spikes as shown in the issue description. The per frame processing time for me is more stable.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3b9c7976-e9d2-4d16-be9e-9eff8cd9f5d0)\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/196ca0d0-bb29-4b33-81f9-4fc0dcc7eed4)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2842356388/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2848818255","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105750#issuecomment-2848818255","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105750","id":2848818255,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pzYRP","user":{"login":"fLindahl","id":18470258,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDcwMjU4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18470258?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl","html_url":"https://github.com/fLindahl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-03T21:35:42Z","updated_at":"2025-05-03T21:35:42Z","body":"Is this a donet problem? I'm running 8.0.408 and I have mega spikes as soon as the GC does a single collect. Haven't had time to test out 9 yet.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2848818255/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2848832187","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105750#issuecomment-2848832187","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105750","id":2848832187,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pzbq7","user":{"login":"Delsin-Yu","id":71481700,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDgxNzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71481700?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu","html_url":"https://github.com/Delsin-Yu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-03T22:13:51Z","updated_at":"2025-05-03T22:15:31Z","body":"> Is this a dotnet problem?\n\nYes and No. In this context, we are deliberately (if not maliciously) overloading the GC by frequently calling expensive APIs or incorrectly using APIs (to demonstrate potential issues a beginner could face). My point is that as an Engine that expects junior developers, some parental precautions should be taken to guide them away from such usages.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2848832187/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2848922394","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105750#issuecomment-2848922394","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105750","id":2848922394,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pzxsa","user":{"login":"MattParkerDev","id":61717342,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxNzE3MzQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61717342?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MattParkerDev","html_url":"https://github.com/MattParkerDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MattParkerDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MattParkerDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MattParkerDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MattParkerDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MattParkerDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MattParkerDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MattParkerDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MattParkerDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MattParkerDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-04T02:39:17Z","updated_at":"2025-05-04T02:39:17Z","body":"Are StringNames for Inputs source generated anywhere? Ie the equivalent of SignalName.MySignalName?\n\nI would be expecting something like `InputMap.Forward`","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2848922394/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2849018435","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105750#issuecomment-2849018435","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105750","id":2849018435,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6p0JJD","user":{"login":"Delsin-Yu","id":71481700,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDgxNzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71481700?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu","html_url":"https://github.com/Delsin-Yu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-04T05:32:54Z","updated_at":"2025-05-04T05:32:54Z","body":"> Are StringNames for Inputs source generated anywhere?\n\nNo, but Cat-Lips' [GodotSharp.SourceGenerators](https://github.com/Cat-Lips/GodotSharp.SourceGenerators) has this feature built-in, I'm also embedding this Library to my project.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2849018435/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2850441140","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105750#issuecomment-2850441140","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105750","id":2850441140,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6p5ke0","user":{"login":"fLindahl","id":18470258,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDcwMjU4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18470258?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl","html_url":"https://github.com/fLindahl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-05T09:33:58Z","updated_at":"2025-05-05T15:20:33Z","body":"> > Is this a dotnet problem?\n> \n> Yes and No. In this context, we are deliberately (if not maliciously) overloading the GC by frequently calling expensive APIs or incorrectly using APIs (to demonstrate potential issues a beginner could face). My point is that as an Engine that expects junior developers, some parental precautions should be taken to guide them away from such usages.\n\nI just tested .net 9, godot 4.4 on Windows 11, and I'm still experiencing stutters when the gc collects. \n\nNot sure if your comment was directed at me specifically (which in that case sounds kind of snarky), but I agree that there should be guides on how to avoid memory allocations in c# (though there's a lot of resources already as you've pointed out). However, I don't think calling something that allocates a small amount of memory per frame should be considered bad practice. Not sure how much time the GC usually takes, but 50ms (edit: this was an exaggeration, but maybe around 20ms?) sounds like more than it's supposed to be. \n\nIs there no possibility that godots .net impl. actually does something that degrades the GC performance (or similar)?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2850441140/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2859195657","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105750#issuecomment-2859195657","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105750","id":2859195657,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6qa90J","user":{"login":"lrahmann","id":9094802,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwOTQ4MDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9094802?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann","html_url":"https://github.com/lrahmann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-07T16:15:40Z","updated_at":"2025-05-07T16:15:40Z","body":"Just happen to find this issue today,\nwe do have a relatively large C# Codebase with Godot and this has been a constant struggle.\n\nThere currently is at least one console platform that will lag even if CoreGC is used instead of BeohmGC(Mono/Unity) because there is no implementation with incremental GC available.\n\nUnity solved part of the lag issue by implementing write barriers to BoehmGC for all platforms which allow for incremental GC.  \n\nThe other thing are the tons of finalizers which Godot is running which are also no free, especially in a concurrent environment.\n\nOur solution at the moment is to reduce the interfacing between C# and Godot to a minimum for non trivial API calls. \nBut especially for arrays and the sort I don't really get while we can't have Godot return Span<T> or ReadOnlySpan<T> and accept them as a argument. This would also mean less memory pressure because right now everything is copied around within these API.\n\nFor the StringName implicit cast issue I was contemplating using something like [ConditionalWeakTable<String,StringName>](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.runtime.compilerservices.conditionalweaktable-2) and add a lookup to the implicit cast. \nUsing a additional **Dictionary<int, WeakReference<StringName>>** it could also be possible to use this cache when having callbacks from the Godot side of things.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2859195657/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2869125672","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105750#issuecomment-2869125672","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105750","id":2869125672,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rA2Io","user":{"login":"Delsin-Yu","id":71481700,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDgxNzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71481700?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu","html_url":"https://github.com/Delsin-Yu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-10T19:36:07Z","updated_at":"2025-05-10T19:36:07Z","body":"@fLindahl \n\n> Not sure if your comment was directed at me specifically\n\nApology for my wording; I do not intend to be rude to people.\n\n> Is there no possibility that godots .net impl. actually does something that degrades the GC performance (or similar)?\n\nGiven the historical reason for the current GodotSharp codebase, it's unlikely we can delete the implicit string name conversions (or redesign the api to accept strings), I hope we can have better choices in the new GDExtension-based bindings.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2869125672/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2972478794","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105750#issuecomment-2972478794","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105750","id":2972478794,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xLG1K","user":{"login":"EricDeng1001","id":28720903,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NzIwOTAz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28720903?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001","html_url":"https://github.com/EricDeng1001","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-14T08:31:34Z","updated_at":"2025-06-14T08:31:34Z","body":"> By the way,\n> \n> > but I'm talking about calling them once per frame.\n> \n> _**ONCE PER FRAME**_ is considered a hot path.\n> \n\nBut many feature DO call api once per frame. It's very normal use case. So it must be performance good.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2972478794/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2972482215","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105750#issuecomment-2972482215","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105750","id":2972482215,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xLHqn","user":{"login":"EricDeng1001","id":28720903,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NzIwOTAz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28720903?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001","html_url":"https://github.com/EricDeng1001","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-14T08:37:48Z","updated_at":"2025-06-14T08:37:48Z","body":"As a UE5 user coming to godot, I never expect a small scene would suffer from such stutter. Godot is very good at fast developing, and many feature, design philosophy is good. But for real production, it has a lot work to do.  I hope godot take C# seriously and really solve this issue.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2972482215/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2974731015","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105750#issuecomment-2974731015","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105750","id":2974731015,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xTssH","user":{"login":"Joy-less","id":65855333,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1ODU1MzMz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65855333?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less","html_url":"https://github.com/Joy-less","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-15T22:44:27Z","updated_at":"2025-06-15T22:44:27Z","body":"> This means an innocuous function such as bool res = Input.IsActionPressed(\"jump\"); might cause stuttering by calling it once per frame, since the string is not actually a regular string, but a StringName that does heap allocations. Of course, you can cache the StringName, and all is fine and dandy, but this is very easy to miss, and will potentially cause stuttering that is almost impossible to find without proper profiling tools (which are somewhat lacking, both in Godot for C# and for dotnet on Linux in general for example).\n\nSee #100452 for a better fix than a Roslyn analyzer.\n\n> This also means that function calls such as this.GetTree().GetNodesInGroup(groupName); will also cause frame time spikes and stutters, since this returns a Godot.Collections.Array that is likely also HAlloc'd.\n\nThis is much more involved to deal with, but every function like this should be changed to return a struct rather than an array. @Delsin-Yu made a related pull request in #106676.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2974731015/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4249995317","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105750#issuecomment-4249995317","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105750","id":4249995317,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc79Ucg1","user":{"login":"Xiexe","id":5119787,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTk3ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5119787?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe","html_url":"https://github.com/Xiexe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-15T07:10:47Z","updated_at":"2026-04-15T07:10:47Z","body":"Just wanting to chime in here to note that my moderately sized C# project is also running into this issue.\n\nIt seems I'm never allowed to allocate *ever* or the GC will take upwards of 50-80ms when it collects.\n\nThis isn't standard across other engines like Unity. Obviously avoiding allocation is good practice, but small allocs shouldn't be triggering a frame drop from over 300 to less than 20 because the GC took so long.\n\nThe whole point of the GC is that it handles this in what should be a generally non intrusive way to the user. \n\nSomething is almost certainly wrong with how it's being handled internally.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4249995317/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4356607475","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105750#issuecomment-4356607475","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105750","id":4356607475,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABA6yN8w","user":{"login":"Xiexe","id":5119787,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTk3ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5119787?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe","html_url":"https://github.com/Xiexe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-30T22:31:41Z","updated_at":"2026-04-30T22:31:41Z","body":"After doing a bit more light digging, there's a few cases where Godot internally missteps.\n\nIn a simple example, you have something like Input.IsActionPressed(\"move_right\") \n\nThis is an example straight from the docs, but internally, this creates a new StringName - which is disposable, but it does not dispose.\n\nThis causes a finalizer to run on the StringName, which causes GC spikes when there is a lot of them to collect (sampling input every frame for instance).\n\nGodot does this all over the place - NodePaths and StringNames are the biggest and easiest offenders to run into. This could be simply fixed by properly disposing of the object internally which calls GC.SuppressFinalize(this), which stops the finalizer from running and stops hitching. \n\nA lot of the time you can work around this stuff manually, but one bad call every frame is all it takes, and it's really easy to mistakenly do, more so than it should be.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4356607475/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4356691155","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105750#issuecomment-4356691155","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105750","id":4356691155,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABA63U0w","user":{"login":"Joy-less","id":65855333,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1ODU1MzMz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65855333?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less","html_url":"https://github.com/Joy-less","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-30T22:50:19Z","updated_at":"2026-04-30T22:50:19Z","body":"@Xiexe Please try my library: https://github.com/Joy-less/GodotStringIntercept\n\nThe library was created specifically to deal with this issue. I am hoping that the library can become Godot's official approach somewhere down the line.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4356691155/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4356727907","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105750#issuecomment-4356727907","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105750","id":4356727907,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABA65kYw","user":{"login":"Xiexe","id":5119787,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTk3ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5119787?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe","html_url":"https://github.com/Xiexe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-30T22:58:00Z","updated_at":"2026-04-30T22:58:00Z","body":"> @Xiexe Please try my library: https://github.com/Joy-less/GodotStringIntercept\n> \n> The library was created specifically to deal with this issue. I am hoping that the library can become Godot's official approach somewhere down the line.\n\nI will give this a look! Thanks!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4356727907/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]